import sys
p = sys.argv[1]
lines = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read().split('\n')
idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('| 673 |')]
assert len(idx) == 1
rows = [
"| 674 | 2026-10-26 | **Stories of music is its own storey in the dollhouse (Build AH).** Built on row 673. Board call 15, changed by her at 14:31 (\"작곡가 스타일 방, 피아노이야기 이런건 다 따로 음악이야기 별도 방에다가\"): The piano's story (was floor 2), Composers and Styles (were on the Grades 2-3 floor) leave the grade floors and sit together on a new PATH_STAGES storey, `stories: true`, between the top floor and the attic, with the theatre wallpaper (`th`). stageExtra() marks the storeys that are not grade floors (the attic, Stories of music): houseFloorsN, houseFloors ('four floors, a Stories of music room and an attic'), floorName ('Stories of music' / '음악 이야기'), the townhouse plaque and 'Next on your path' (the last room in Stories of music, not 'floor 5') follow it. The Lesson Book's small house breaks a long storey name before its last word. Chapter numbers follow the new order (Key signatures 21 ... Melody 29, The piano 30, Composers 31, Styles 32, Pitch 33). Call 14 decided at the same time: the four Grades 2-3 rooms in the recommended order (Hear, sing, write; Scales; Intervals and chords further; Reading and rhythm further); call 13 (14:26): no exercises room, the exam's exercises (1A-1C, 2A-3C) stay with the book and the teacher. Files: drills.html, drills.src.html, _workspace/concept-book-kit/sc/patch698.py. |",
"| 675 | 2026-10-26 | **Workbooks and teacher's copies for the new rooms (Build AI-1 to AI-4).** Built on row 674. The board's queue item, her 14:31 \"응\". Playing Scales (SpWorkbook, SpTeacher), Minor Scales (MsWorkbook, MsTeacher) and 6/8 Time (E8Workbook, E8Teacher): pages 2 to 6 face the Lesson Book's steps (try it, your turn, play), page 7 is the check-up on paper facing My five checks, and the teacher's copy has every answer, what to watch for, what to say and the scoring (4 marks a part, pass 3+, go back to the step's page). Every answer is computed from the room's own data (spFing, spCm, spThumbs, msNames, MS_REL, MS_GAPS, E8, E8_FILL, rq68Count), so paper and app cannot disagree; all were checked by hand against the scale and rhythm data. Listen, Clap, Write and Listen and Sing get a teacher's copy only (every step is by ear): the material to play, taken from the rooms' own lists (LW_HOME, LW_CLAP, LW_PH, LW_DICTS, LS_ECHO, LS_SING), in her words (walk, run-ning, hold; the bird and the turtle). Tests: book sweep (work, teacher, spread for nine chapters, no errors, no overflow), chapter sweep (33 chapters, learn and drill, en/ko), full Home regression. Files: drills.html, drills.src.html, _workspace/concept-book-kit/sc/patch699.py to patch702.py. |",
]
for r in reversed(rows): lines.insert(idx[0] + 1, r)
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write('\n'.join(lines)); print('ok')
